    "text": "A plane passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> contains two lines whose direction ratios are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> respectively. If, this plane also passes through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to",
